{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cge36T7VjabwjjRM6YCCc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vk9et6e3B7gRYLLmCybQXk","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"status":"done","summary":"Added truncation warnings for text filters with more than 5 search terms (Redmine #44464). The tokenizer now exposes MAX_TOKENS and truncated?, Query#filter_warnings returns one message per truncated filter, and the issue list query form, calendar and Gantt show them as <p class=\"warning\"> above the results, with the terms HTML-escaped. Results are still shown and the query stays valid. Tests were added at unit and functional level. The full non-system suite (bin/rails test) passes: 6091 runs, 0 failures, 0 errors, 37 skips. Nothing was committed or pushed.","changes":[{"path":"lib/redmine/search.rb","summary":"Tokenizer: MAX_TOKENS = 5 constant, tokens returns at most MAX_TOKENS (computed from a private all_tokens list), new truncated? method true when there are more than MAX_TOKENS terms."},{"path":"app/models/query.rb","summary":"New filter_warnings method. For string/text/search filters with operator ~, *~, !~, ^ or $, it tokenizes value.first and returns a localized message per truncated filter. Constants TOKENIZED_OPERATORS and TOKENIZED_FILTER_TYPES. Terms are quoted and joined with support.array.words_connector."},{"path":"config/locales/en.yml","summary":"Added notice_search_terms_truncated with the English message text (%{filter}, %{max}, %{terms})."},{"path":"app/views/queries/_filter_warnings.html.erb","summary":"New partial rendering each query.filter_warnings message as <p class=\"warning\"> (ERB-escaped)."},{"path":"app/views/queries/_query_form.html.erb","summary":"Renders the filter warnings partial after error_messages_for (issue list and other lists using the query form)."},{"path":"app/views/gantts/show.html.erb","summary":"Renders the filter warnings partial above the Gantt chart."},{"pat